# Cross-course AP exam language — master IDs CORE-001..097. Also used by the Question Decoder.
# Command-verb meanings summarize common AP task-verb usage; check each course's CED for subject-specific expectations.
@subject ap-exam-language | AP Exam Language | AP 考试通用语言 | Exam English | gold | 0
@desc The command verbs, connectors and reasoning words that appear across every AP exam.
@framework Command verbs are summarized from task-verb guidance published in AP course and exam descriptions; meanings can vary slightly by course.

@unit 1 | Command Verbs | 题目指令动词
@topic 1.1 | Name and Report | 指出与陈述 | Recognize verbs that ask for short answers
- identify | 识别；指出 | Name or select the requested feature without extended explanation | 只需指出或选出答案，不需要解释原因。写一句话即可，过多解释不会额外得分。 | Identify one factor that shifts the demand curve. | 1 | #CORE-001
  cat: Exam command verb
  vs: explain
- state | 陈述 | Give a concise answer without additional reasoning unless requested | 直接给出结论或数值，一般不需要推理过程。 | State the null hypothesis for the test. | 1 | #CORE-002
  cat: Exam command verb
- define | 定义 | Give the precise meaning of a term | 给出术语的准确含义，最好用课程中的标准表述。 | Define opportunity cost. | 1 | #CORE-003
  cat: Exam command verb
- describe | 描述 | Report the relevant characteristics or what happens, without necessarily explaining why | 说明“是什么、怎么样”（特征、过程、趋势），通常不要求解释“为什么”。 | Describe the trend in the data from 1990 to 2010. | 2 | #CORE-004
  cat: Exam command verb
  vs: explain
- label | 标注 | Name the relevant parts of a diagram or graph | 在图上标出相关部分（坐标轴、曲线、均衡点等）。 | Label the equilibrium price and quantity on the graph. | 1 | #CORE-027
  cat: Exam command verb
- outline | 概述 | Present the main stages or features without full detail | 列出主要步骤或要点，不必展开细节。 | Outline the stages of mitosis. | 2 | #CORE-030
  cat: Exam command verb
- summarize | 总结 | Present the main ideas concisely | 简洁地概括主要内容。 | Summarize the author's main argument. | 1 | #CORE-023
  cat: Exam command verb
- classify | 分类 | Assign something to a category based on relevant features | 根据相关特征把对象归入某一类别。 | Classify each variable as categorical or quantitative. | 2 | #CORE-024
  cat: Exam command verb
@topic 1.2 | Reason and Explain | 推理与解释 | Recognize verbs that require reasoning
- explain | 解释 | Show how or why something happens using reasoning, often linking cause and effect | 说明“如何”或“为什么”，要有因果链条（因为……所以……），不能只给结论。 | Explain why a binding price ceiling causes a shortage. | 2 | #CORE-005
  cat: Exam command verb
  mis: Explain means restate the answer — you must give the reasoning that connects evidence to the conclusion.
  vs: describe; identify
- justify | 论证；证明合理性 | Support an answer with evidence or reasoning | 用证据、数据或原理支持你的答案。 | Justify your answer using the value of the derivative. | 2 | #CORE-010
  cat: Exam command verb
- account for | 解释原因 | Explain the cause or reason for an outcome | 解释某个结果产生的原因。 | Account for the decline in population after 1350. | 2 | #CORE-032
  cat: Exam command verb
- predict | 预测 | State an expected outcome based on a model or evidence | 根据模型或证据说明预期的结果，常需附带理由。 | Predict the effect of an increase in temperature on enzyme activity. | 2 | #CORE-016
  cat: Exam command verb
- infer | 推断 | Draw a conclusion supported by available information | 根据现有信息合理地推出结论。 | What can be inferred from the data about the relationship? | 2 | #CORE-017
  cat: Exam command verb
- interpret | 解读 | Explain the meaning of information in context | 在具体情境中说明数值、图表或史料的含义（例如解释斜率的现实意义）。 | Interpret the slope of the regression line in context. | 2 | #CORE-009
  cat: Exam command verb
- analyze | 分析 | Break information into its parts, relationships and mechanisms | 把信息分解为组成部分并说明它们之间的关系和作用机制。 | Analyze how the author's purpose affects the reliability of the source. | 3 | #CORE-008
  cat: Exam command verb
- distinguish | 区分 | Explain how two ideas are different | 说明两个概念之间的不同之处。 | Distinguish between diffusion and osmosis. | 2 | #CORE-031
  cat: Exam command verb
- compare | 比较 | Identify relevant similarities and differences | 指出相关的相同点和不同点（AP 历史中常要求两者都有）。 | Compare the methods used by the Ottoman and Mughal empires to legitimize rule. | 2 | #CORE-011
  cat: Exam command verb
  vs: contrast
- contrast | 对比 | Identify meaningful differences | 强调不同点。 | Contrast the economic policies of two administrations. | 2 | #CORE-012
  cat: Exam command verb
  vs: compare
@topic 1.3 | Judge and Argue | 评价与论证 | Recognize verbs that require judgment
- evaluate | 评价；评估 | Judge a claim using evidence and criteria | 依据证据和标准对观点的合理性或程度做出判断，需要考虑支持与反对两方面。 | Evaluate the extent to which the New Deal changed the role of government. | 3 | #CORE-006
  cat: Exam command verb
- assess | 评估 | Weigh the importance or validity of a claim | 权衡观点的重要性或有效性。 | Assess the reliability of the source. | 3 | #CORE-007
  cat: Exam command verb
- to what extent | 在多大程度上 | Judge how far a claim is valid | 不仅回答“是不是”，还要判断“程度有多大”，通常需要承认反例或局限。 | To what extent did industrialization change gender roles? | 3 | #CORE-033
  cat: Exam command verb
- support | 支持；论证 | Provide evidence for a claim | 给出支持某观点的证据。 | Use evidence to support the claim that trade networks expanded. | 2 | #CORE-018
  cat: Exam command verb
- refute | 反驳 | Use evidence or reasoning against a claim | 用证据或推理反驳某一观点。 | Provide evidence that could refute the historian's argument. | 2 | #CORE-019
  cat: Exam command verb
- qualify | 限定；修正 | Add conditions or limitations to a claim | 为观点增加条件或限制（“在某些情况下成立”）。注意它不是“合格”的意思。 | Qualify the claim by explaining one exception. | 3 | #CORE-020
  cat: Exam command verb
  mis: Qualify means "to be good enough" — in AP writing it means to limit or add conditions to a claim.
- corroborate | 佐证 | Confirm a claim using independent evidence | 用另一份独立证据证实某一说法。 | Identify a document that corroborates the author's account. | 3 | #CORE-021
  cat: Exam command verb
- synthesize | 综合 | Combine information into a coherent interpretation | 把多个来源的信息整合成一个连贯的解释或论点。 | Synthesize evidence from at least four documents. | 3 | #CORE-022
  cat: Exam command verb
@topic 1.4 | Calculate and Represent | 计算与表示 | Recognize verbs for quantitative and visual tasks
- calculate | 计算 | Use mathematical operations to obtain a result, showing work | 通过运算得出结果，一般要写出过程和单位。 | Calculate the price elasticity of demand. | 1 | #CORE-013
  cat: Exam command verb
- determine | 确定 | Find a result from evidence or a method | 根据证据或方法确定答案，可能需要计算或推理。 | Determine whether the series converges. | 2 | #CORE-014
  cat: Exam command verb
- estimate | 估计 | Find an approximate value | 求近似值，需说明方法。 | Estimate f′(3) using the data in the table. | 2 | #CORE-015
  cat: Exam command verb
- construct | 构建 | Create a graph, model, explanation or representation | 建立图表、模型或论证。 | Construct a 95% confidence interval. | 2 | #CORE-025
  cat: Exam command verb
- sketch | 绘制草图 | Draw a simplified representation showing key features | 画出能显示关键特征的简图，不需要精确比例。 | Sketch the graph of a function with a local maximum at x = 2. | 1 | #CORE-026
  cat: Exam command verb
- plot | 绘图；标点 | Place values or points on a graph | 在坐标系中画出数据点。 | Plot the data on the axes provided. | 1 | #CORE-028
  cat: Exam command verb
- illustrate | 举例说明 | Clarify a point with an example or diagram | 用例子或图示说明观点。 | Illustrate your answer with a specific example. | 2 | #CORE-029
  cat: Exam command verb

@unit 2 | Reading and Writing Connectors | 阅读与写作连接词
@topic 2.1 | Source and Context | 出处与语境 | Recognize phrases that restrict what evidence to use
- according to | 根据 | Base the answer on a named source | 答案必须依据指定的材料。 | According to the passage, what caused the decline? | 1 | #CORE-034
  cat: Logical connector
- based on | 基于 | Use the given information as the foundation | 以题目给出的信息为基础作答。 | Based on the graph, which year had the highest output? | 1 | #CORE-035
  cat: Logical connector
- with reference to | 结合；参照 | Use a specified example or source | 要结合指定的例子或材料。 | With reference to Document 2, explain the author's view. | 2 | #CORE-036
  cat: Logical connector
- in the context of | 在……背景下 | Interpret a claim within its situation | 在特定情境或背景中理解。 | Interpret the result in the context of the study. | 2 | #CORE-037
  cat: Logical connector
@topic 2.2 | Cause, Result and Contrast | 因果与转折 | Track logical direction in a sentence
- as a result | 因此；结果 | Introduces an outcome caused by earlier events | 引出前面事件导致的结果。 | Prices rose; as a result, quantity demanded fell. | 1 | #CORE-038
  cat: Logical connector
- therefore | 因此 | Introduces a conclusion drawn from preceding reasoning | 引出由前面推理得到的结论。 | The limit exists; therefore, f is continuous if f(a) equals it. | 1 | #CORE-039
  cat: Logical connector
- consequently | 因此 | Shows a resulting effect | 表示由此产生的结果。 | Consequently, the population declined. | 2 | #CORE-040
  cat: Logical connector
- thus | 因此 | Introduces a logical conclusion | 引出逻辑结论，常用于数学和科学写作。 | Thus, the series converges. | 1 | #CORE-041
  cat: Logical connector
- because | 因为 | Introduces a reason or cause | 引出原因。 | The cell shrank because water left by osmosis. | 1 | #CORE-042
  cat: Logical connector
- since | 由于；自从 | Indicates a cause, or a starting time, depending on context | 可表示原因（由于），也可表示时间（自从），要根据上下文判断。 | Since 1945, many colonies have gained independence. | 2 | #CORE-043
  cat: Logical connector
- due to | 由于 | Indicates a cause | 由于（后接名词短语）。 | The shortage was due to a price ceiling. | 1 | #CORE-044
  cat: Logical connector
- owing to | 由于 | Indicates a cause | 由于（较正式）。 | Owing to drought, harvests failed. | 2 | #CORE-045
  cat: Logical connector
- whereas | 然而；而 | Contrasts two statements | 表示对比：一方……而另一方……。 | Mitosis produces identical cells, whereas meiosis produces unique gametes. | 2 | #CORE-046
  cat: Logical connector
- while | 虽然；当……时 | Shows contrast or simultaneous time | 可表示对比（虽然、而），也可表示时间（当……时）。 | While prices rose, wages stayed flat. | 2 | #CORE-047
  cat: Logical connector
- although | 虽然 | Introduces a concession | 引出让步：虽然……但……。英文中不与 but 同时使用。 | Although the empire was large, it was difficult to govern. | 1 | #CORE-048
  cat: Logical connector
- nevertheless | 然而；尽管如此 | Introduces a contrasting point despite earlier information | 尽管如此（表示转折）。 | The policy was unpopular; nevertheless, it passed. | 2 | #CORE-049
  cat: Logical connector
- however | 然而 | Introduces contrast or a limitation | 然而，表示转折或限制。 | However, the evidence is limited to one region. | 1 | #CORE-050
  cat: Logical connector
- in contrast | 相比之下 | Marks a difference between cases | 相比之下，表示两者不同。 | In contrast, Japan industrialized rapidly. | 1 | #CORE-051
  cat: Logical connector
- on the contrary | 恰恰相反 | Introduces an opposing claim | 恰恰相反（否定前面的说法）。 | The reform did not weaken the state; on the contrary, it strengthened it. | 2 | #CORE-096
  cat: Logical connector
- notwithstanding | 尽管 | Despite a stated circumstance | 尽管（正式用语）。 | Notwithstanding these limits, the study is useful. | 3 | #CORE-097
  cat: Logical connector
- rather than | 而不是 | Indicates a preferred or contrasted alternative | 而不是，表示选择或对比。 | The firm chose to expand rather than merge. | 1 | #CORE-060
  cat: Logical connector
@topic 2.3 | Adding, Examples and Precision | 补充、举例与精确 | Recognize words that add or narrow information
- similarly | 类似地 | Introduces a shared feature | 类似地。 | Similarly, the Mughals used religious tolerance. | 1 | #CORE-052
  cat: Logical connector
- likewise | 同样地 | Indicates a parallel case | 同样地。 | Likewise, prices fell in the second market. | 1 | #CORE-053
  cat: Logical connector
- moreover | 此外 | Adds supporting information | 此外，而且（补充更有力的信息）。 | Moreover, the data show a strong correlation. | 1 | #CORE-054
  cat: Logical connector
- furthermore | 此外 | Adds another supporting point | 此外，再者。 | Furthermore, the treaty expanded trade. | 1 | #CORE-055
  cat: Logical connector
- in addition | 此外 | Adds information | 另外。 | In addition, the cell requires ATP. | 1 | #CORE-056
  cat: Logical connector
- for instance | 例如 | Introduces an example | 例如。 | Some goods are inferior; for instance, instant noodles. | 1 | #CORE-057
  cat: Logical connector
- specifically | 具体而言 | Narrows a statement to precise details | 具体来说，把陈述缩小到具体细节。 | Specifically, explain the role of the active site. | 2 | #CORE-058
  cat: Logical connector
- respectively | 分别地 | Matches items in the order listed | 按前面列举的顺序一一对应。 | Groups A and B scored 80 and 90, respectively. | 2 | #CORE-059
  cat: Logical connector
@topic 2.4 | Conditions and Quantities | 条件与数量 | Read conditions and bounds precisely
- provided that | 只要；前提是 | States a necessary condition | 只要……；前提是……。 | The theorem applies provided that f is continuous. | 2 | #CORE-061
  cat: Logical connector
- unless | 除非 | Introduces an exception or condition | 除非……（否则……）。 | The object keeps moving unless a net force acts. | 1 | #CORE-062
  cat: Logical connector
- if and only if | 当且仅当 | Expresses a condition that is both necessary and sufficient | 充要条件：两个方向都成立。 | A series converges if and only if its partial sums converge. | 3 | #CORE-063
  cat: Logical connector
- at least | 至少 | Gives a lower bound | 至少（≥）。 | At least one solution exists. | 1 | #CORE-064
  cat: Logical connector
- at most | 至多 | Gives an upper bound | 至多（≤）。 | The cubic has at most three real zeros. | 1 | #CORE-065
  cat: Logical connector
- approximately | 大约 | Indicates an estimated value | 大约，近似。 | The population is approximately 3,000. | 1 | #CORE-066
  cat: Logical connector
- proportional to | 与……成正比 | Changes at a constant ratio with another quantity | 与……成正比：一个变为几倍，另一个也变为几倍。 | Kinetic energy is proportional to the square of speed. | 2 | #CORE-067
  cat: Logical connector
  vs: inversely proportional
- inversely proportional | 与……成反比 | Varies so that the product of two quantities is constant | 成反比：一个变为 2 倍，另一个变为一半。 | Gravitational force is inversely proportional to distance squared. | 2 | #CORE-068
  cat: Logical connector
  vs: proportional to
- increase by | 增加了 | Indicates the amount of change | 增加了（表示增加的量）。 | Sales increased by 20 units (from 100 to 120). | 1 | #CORE-069
  cat: Logical connector
  vs: increase to
- increase to | 增加到 | Indicates the final level | 增加到（表示最终达到的值）。 | Sales increased to 120 units. | 1 | #CORE-070
  cat: Logical connector
  vs: increase by
- decrease by | 减少了 | Indicates the amount of reduction | 减少了（减少的量）。 | The price decreased by $2. | 1 | #CORE-071
  cat: Logical connector
- decrease to | 减少到 | Indicates the final lower level | 减少到（最终值）。 | The price decreased to $8. | 1 | #CORE-072
  cat: Logical connector
- relative to | 相对于 | Expressed in comparison with another value | 相对于（与另一个值比较）。 | The dollar appreciated relative to the euro. | 2 | #CORE-095
  cat: Logical connector
- independent of | 独立于 | Not dependent on another factor | 与……无关，不受……影响。 | A pendulum's period is independent of its mass. | 2 | #CORE-073
  cat: Logical connector
- prior to | 在……之前 | Occurring before a specified event | 在……之前（正式）。 | Prior to 1492, the Americas were isolated from Afro-Eurasia. | 1 | #CORE-094
  cat: Logical connector
- subsequent | 随后的 | Occurring later in a sequence | 随后的，之后的。 | Subsequent reforms expanded voting rights. | 2 | #CORE-093
  cat: Logical connector

@unit 3 | Academic Reasoning | 学术推理
@topic 3.1 | Claims and Evidence | 论点与证据 | Use reasoning vocabulary precisely
- claim | 论点；主张 | A statement presented for evaluation or defense | 需要用证据支持的观点或主张。 | Make a claim that answers the question directly. | 1 | #CORE-079
  cat: Academic language
- evidence | 证据 | Information used to support a conclusion | 用来支持结论的信息（数据、史料、实验结果）。 | Cite two pieces of evidence from the documents. | 1 | #CORE-080
  cat: Academic language
- reasoning | 推理 | The logical steps linking evidence to a conclusion | 把证据和结论连接起来的逻辑步骤。 | Your reasoning should explain why the evidence supports the claim. | 2 | #CORE-081
  cat: Academic language
- hypothesis | 假设 | A testable proposed explanation | 可以被检验的解释性假说。 | The hypothesis predicts that light intensity affects photosynthesis rate. | 2 | #CORE-078
  cat: Academic language
  vs: assume
- assume | 假设 | Treat a condition as true for the purpose of analysis | 为分析而假定某条件成立。 | Assume that air resistance is negligible. | 2 | #CORE-077
  cat: Academic language
  vs: hypothesis
- imply | 意味着；暗示 | Suggest a logical consequence | 暗含，意味着。 | A negative slope implies an inverse relationship. | 2 | #CORE-076
  cat: Academic language
- consistent with | 与……一致 | Agrees with a model or evidence | 与……一致，不矛盾（但不等于证明）。 | The results are consistent with the hypothesis. | 2 | #CORE-074
  cat: Academic language
  vs: contradict
- contradict | 与……矛盾 | Conflict with a claim or result | 与……相矛盾。 | The new evidence contradicts the earlier theory. | 2 | #CORE-075
  cat: Academic language
  vs: consistent with
- limitation | 局限性 | A restriction on what a method or result establishes | 方法或结论的局限。 | One limitation is the small sample size. | 2 | #CORE-082
  cat: Academic language
- bias | 偏差；偏见 | A systematic distortion or predisposition | 系统性的偏差或偏见（统计中的偏差，史料中的立场偏见）。 | The survey's wording introduced bias. | 2 | #CORE-083
  cat: Academic language
- underlying | 根本的；潜在的 | Existing beneath the visible explanation | 深层的、根本的（原因）。 | The underlying cause of the war was economic rivalry. | 2 | #CORE-092
  cat: Academic language
- ambiguous | 模糊的；有歧义的 | Open to more than one interpretation | 可以有多种理解的。 | The question's wording is ambiguous. | 2 | #CORE-091
  cat: Academic language
@topic 3.2 | Data Words | 数据用语 | Read data vocabulary precisely
- variable | 变量 | A quantity or characteristic that can vary | 可以变化的量或特征。 | Temperature is the variable being tested. | 1 | #CORE-084
  cat: Academic language
- trend | 趋势 | A general direction of change | 总体变化方向。 | The data show an upward trend. | 1 | #CORE-085
  cat: Academic language
- correlation | 相关性 | A statistical association between variables | 变量之间的统计关联，不等于因果关系。 | There is a strong positive correlation between study time and scores. | 2 | #CORE-086
  cat: Academic language
  vs: causation
- causation | 因果关系 | A relationship in which one factor produces an effect | 一个因素导致另一个结果的关系。 | Only a controlled experiment can establish causation. | 2 | #CORE-087
  cat: Academic language
  vs: correlation
- significant | 显著的；重要的 | Meaningful in context; statistical significance requires a defined test | 日常是“重要的”，统计中“显著”需要有明确的检验标准。 | The difference was statistically significant at α = 0.05. | 2 | #CORE-088
  cat: Academic language
- valid | 有效的 | Well-supported or appropriate for its intended purpose | 有充分依据的，或测量了它想测量的东西。 | A valid test measures what it claims to measure. | 2 | #CORE-089
  cat: Academic language
  vs: reliable
- reliable | 可靠的 | Consistent or dependable under repeated use | 重复使用时结果一致、稳定。 | A reliable scale gives the same reading each time. | 2 | #CORE-090
  cat: Academic language
  vs: valid

@q core-u1-001 | UNDERSTAND | CONCEPT | SCENARIO | 1 | 2 | explain; describe
? A question says "Explain why the price rose." Which response best meets the command?
= "The price rose from $4 to $6." :: That describes what happened but gives no reason.
=* "Demand increased while supply stayed the same, so at the old price there was a shortage, which pushed the price up." :: Correct — it gives a cause-and-effect chain.
= "Price." :: That does not answer the question.
= "The graph shows a rise." :: Pointing to the graph is not an explanation.
! "Explain" requires reasoning: connect causes to the outcome with because/so logic.
!zh “Explain” 要求说明原因：用“因为……所以……”把原因和结果连接起来。
@q core-u1-002 | UNDERSTAND | CONCEPT | MCQ | 1 | 2 | identify; explain
? Which task requires the SHORTEST acceptable response?
=* Identify one cause of the Black Death's spread. :: Correct — naming the cause is enough.
= Explain how trade routes spread the Black Death. :: Requires reasoning.
= Evaluate the extent to which the Black Death changed Europe. :: Requires judgment with evidence.
= Compare the Black Death's effects in Europe and Asia. :: Requires similarities and differences.
! Identify/state = name it. Explain = show how or why. Evaluate = judge with evidence.
!zh Identify/State 只需指出；Explain 需说明如何/为什么；Evaluate 需用证据做判断。
@q core-u2-001 | UNDERSTAND | CONCEPT | CLOZE | 2 | 1 | increase by; increase to
? Sales went from 100 to 150. Sales increased ______ 50 units.
a: by
! "Increase by" gives the amount of change; "increase to" gives the final value (150).
!zh increase by 表示增加的量（50）；increase to 表示最终值（150）。

@pair compare-vs-contrast | compare | contrast
! "Compare" asks for similarities AND differences; "contrast" focuses on differences.
!zh compare 要求相同点和不同点；contrast 侧重不同点。
s: A :: Discuss how two empires were alike and how they differed. :: Both similarities and differences.
s: B :: Explain how the two policies differed. :: Only differences.
s: A :: Identify one similarity and one difference. :: Classic compare task.
s: B :: Highlight what makes the second source unlike the first. :: Differences only.
@pair describe-vs-explain | describe | explain
! "Describe" says WHAT happens; "explain" says WHY or HOW it happens.
!zh describe 说明“是什么”；explain 说明“为什么/如何”。
s: A :: "The graph rises steeply from 2000 to 2010." :: Reports what happens.
s: B :: "The graph rises because new technology lowered costs." :: Gives a reason.
s: B :: "This occurs because water moves toward higher solute concentration." :: Causal reasoning.
s: A :: "The cell becomes smaller and its membrane pulls away from the wall." :: Reports features.
@pair correlation-causation | correlation | causation
! Correlation is an association between variables; causation means one variable produces a change in another. Correlation alone does not prove causation.
!zh 相关是变量间的关联；因果是一个变量导致另一个变化。相关不等于因果。
s: A :: Students who sleep more tend to have higher grades. :: Association only.
s: B :: Randomly assigned students given tutoring scored higher than controls. :: Experiment supports causation.
s: A :: Countries with more TVs have longer life expectancy. :: A lurking variable (wealth) is likely.
s: B :: Increasing the dose in a controlled trial lowered blood pressure. :: Controlled manipulation.
@pair valid-vs-reliable | valid | reliable
! Reliable = consistent results; valid = measures what it is supposed to measure. A measure can be reliable without being valid.
!zh 可靠 = 结果一致；有效 = 测到了想测的东西。可靠不一定有效。
s: B :: A scale always reads 2 kg too heavy, but gives the same number every time. :: Consistent but wrong.
s: A :: A reading test that truly measures comprehension. :: Measures the intended construct.
s: B :: Repeating the survey a week later gives the same results. :: Consistency.
s: A :: An IQ test that predicts school performance well. :: Measures what it claims.
